  "delivery": {
    "targetWordsPerMinute": 149,
    "inputWordsPerMinute": 175.24,
    "tempo": 0.87188056,
    "outputWordsPerMinute": 148.99
  },
  "audioSha256": "cf3cc7876a33b5730e9f386ce0d6ee46638335229273993baa0ea4d3d7683780",
  "captionsSha256": "3bbda0d1a86d3d3aee7754acbef21cd905ddd8d89a06d22bfbda077862d55e57",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "baseline",
      "scriptSha256": "e49c6efb1166c252844c1623305a8bd0848e090286efcf5d30d2bb685689324d",
      "durationFrames": 578,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.362,
          "end": 2.662,
          "text": "Ask “Why does zero pass validation?”"
        },
        {
          "start": 3.466,
          "end": 6.052,
          "text": "in a fresh chat. Depending on the\nsession,"
        },
        {
          "start": 6.294,
          "end": 11.41,
          "text": "Copilot may already receive parts of the\nactive editor or search the workspace."
        },
        {
          "start": 11.846,
          "end": 16.8,
          "text": "Look for the sources cited in its\nanswer. Even a correct guess is easier"
        },
        {
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 19.546,
          "text": "to evaluate once you know where it came\nfrom."
        },
        {
          "start": 20.041,
          "end": 22.681,
          "text": "Next we will choose the evidence\ndeliberately."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "needed",
      "scriptSha256": "57c328dba39629b3dc49c916e7b51bc0c1d9c1d76cbf8f0171c469502830caac",
      "durationFrames": 511,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.315,
          "end": 5.068,
          "text": "Select three things from the training\ncheckout. The issue tells you what"
        },
        {
          "start": 5.068,
          "end": 5.683,
          "text": "should happen."
        },
        {
          "start": 6.223,
          "end": 8.914,
          "text": "The validator tells you what the program\ndoes now."
        },
        {
          "start": 9.259,
          "end": 12.455,
          "text": "The test file tells you what behavior is\nalready covered."
        },
        {
          "start": 12.87,
          "end": 15.698,
          "text": "If you only have the issue, you can\nexplain the rule."
        },
        {
          "start": 16.021,
          "end": 20.181,
          "text": "With the source, you can identify\nexactly which comparison breaks it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "attach",
      "scriptSha256": "fba5ac4aaa4f40d42ec4468f20b9cee259bdfb63b58a23614d9034bdab062808",
      "durationFrames": 530,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.315,
          "end": 3.434,
          "text": "Open the validator and the test file in\nVS Code."
        },
        {
          "start": 4.112,
          "end": 7.004,
          "text": "Use the chat attachment control to add\nthose files."
        },
        {
          "start": 7.569,
          "end": 11.64,
          "text": "Include the synthetic issue text and\ninspect the list before sending."
        },
        {
          "start": 11.987,
          "end": 15.393,
          "text": "Confirm the paths are from the checkout\nyou intend to work on."
        },
        {
          "start": 15.715,
          "end": 20.495,
          "text": "This lets you and the assistant refer to\nthe same function and the same tests."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "inspect",
      "scriptSha256": "f93c8ab4f881c65b1d71f3ddb720758f899185e30a8619721dd593b9a3f28fd6",
      "durationFrames": 573,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.361,
          "end": 3.958,
          "text": "Ask two questions together. “Why does\nzero pass,"
        },
        {
          "start": 4.499,
          "end": 6.51,
          "text": "and which baseline test covers it?”"
        },
        {
          "start": 7.152,
          "end": 11.754,
          "text": "The answer should show that greater than\nor equal to zero returns true for zero."
        },
        {
          "start": 12.075,
          "end": 17.03,
          "text": "Read the tests for one, five, and\nnegative one. None runs the zero case."
        },
        {
          "start": 17.593,
          "end": 21.985,
          "text": "That gap explains why the existing suite\ncan be green while the issue remains"
        },
        {
          "start": 21.997,
          "end": 22.647,
          "text": "open.",
          "speechEnd": 22.331
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "prune",
      "scriptSha256": "27bedbc6123f7dc00d1806e453e8a6f33dc2c2cdd1d3fe3dd5183d32d28f34ec",
      "durationFrames": 594,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.339,
          "end": 4.108,
          "text": "Imagine an older attachment shows a\ngreater-than comparison."
        },
        {
          "start": 4.545,
          "end": 8.003,
          "text": "The active checkout still has greater\nthan or equal to zero."
        },
        {
          "start": 8.394,
          "end": 10.958,
          "text": "Open the current file and confirm the\nbranch,"
        },
        {
          "start": 11.246,
          "end": 13.166,
          "text": "then remove the stale attachment."
        },
        {
          "start": 13.683,
          "end": 16.185,
          "text": "Ask the question again using the current\nsource."
        },
        {
          "start": 16.771,
          "end": 20.067,
          "text": "A one-character difference is enough to\nchange the answer,"
        },
        {
          "start": 20.514,
          "end": 23.259,
          "text": "so keep the two versions easy to\ndistinguish."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "followup",
      "scriptSha256": "b35cb238fe2ff1e7df998acf805e27a06d6a965392d052e1c9a083f7602a6e0a",
      "durationFrames": 550,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.292,
          "end": 4.509,
          "text": "Try a follow-up where you provide the\nfunction but leave out the issue."
        },
        {
          "start": 5.049,
          "end": 9.262,
          "text": "Ask what the program does and what\nevidence would tell you whether that is"
        },
        {
          "start": 9.262,
          "end": 9.912,
          "text": "correct.",
          "speechEnd": 9.787
        },
        {
          "start": 10.304,
          "end": 14.271,
          "text": "The code answers the first question. The\nissue answers the second."
        },
        {
          "start": 14.846,
          "end": 19.18,
          "text": "After you provide it, ask the assistant\nto compare the two and check that it"
        },
        {
          "start": 19.18,
          "end": 21.425,
          "text": "keeps both claims tied to their sources."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "practice",
      "scriptSha256": "856829eaf3f8a9ba504689d568bb6518e1c51ab58cae95147948a67eaeab981b",
      "durationFrames": 530,
      "cues": [
        {
          "start": 0.292,
          "end": 3.897,
          "text": "Run the same question in two fresh\nsessions on the same branch."
        },
        {
          "start": 4.483,
          "end": 9.319,
          "text": "In the first attach the issue alone. In\nthe second add the validator and tests."
        },
        {
          "start": 9.802,
          "end": 12.744,
          "text": "Compare their claims about the cause and\ncoverage."
        },
        {
          "start": 13.308,
          "end": 18.234,
          "text": "Look for a real source line and a named\ntest. Write one sentence about which"
        },
        {
          "start": 18.234,
          "end": 20.608,
          "text": "attachment made each claim checkable."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
